      "id": "a4197e4a-56c2-454e-b103-efa1f6fa9959",
      "name": "Code in JavaScript"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "modelId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "models/gemini-3.8-flash",
          "mode": "list",
          "cachedResultName": "models/gemini-3.8-flash"
        },
        "messages": {
          "values": [
            {
              "content": "<Task>  \nGenerate a daily weather message, in English, summarizing the forecast for today.  \n</Task>  \n\n<Goal>  \n- Open with an overview of the weather across Portugal.  \n- Include national weather patterns, highlighting the expected minimum and maximum temperatures and where they will be observed.  \n- Mention active weather warnings and the most important expected impact.  \n- Then provide details for Lisbon and Leiria.  \n- End with a short practical recommendation only if it makes sense.  \n</Goal>  \n\n<Rules>  \n- Prioritize real active warnings.  \n- Do not invent values or descriptions.  \n- If there are no warnings, say “No relevant weather warnings today” or a natural equivalent.  \n- Summarize national patterns concisely without listing too many locations, but always include the national minimum and maximum temperatures and their locations.  \n- Clearly separate the national overview from the Lisbon and Leiria details with a paragraph break.  \n- For Lisbon and Leiria, mention sky conditions, minimum and maximum temperatures, precipitation probability, and wind, if available.  \n- If there is relevant local risk, highlight it.  \n- Keep the message natural, concise, and ready to send.  \n- No markdown, no bullet points, no JSON, no headings.  \n</Rules>  \n\n<Output>  \nReturn only the final message text.  \n</Output>"
            },
            {
              "content": "=<Data>\n{{ JSON.stringify($json.weather_data) }}\n</Data> "
            }
          ]
        },
        "simplify": false,
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are a weather assistant for Portugal. Your task is to generate a daily message, in English, based on IPMA data.",
          "candidateCount": 1,
          "maxToolsIterations": 2
        }
      },
